unt. It rolls up to nothing, and it is neither a shipping site nor a bill-to party."}, {"rule": "tw:DeliveredLoadShape", "statement": "A load is delivered when the carrier on its final row reports the final delivery: status DLVD. A canceled load does not count as delivered."}, {"rule": "tw:InvoiceNeedsSignedProofShape", "statement": "A load can be invoiced only when a signed proof of delivery is on file. An unsigned document does not count."}, {"rule": "tw:LoadBelongsToParentShape", "statement": "Revenue and loads belong to the parent of the site that shipped."}, {"rule": "tw:LoadBookedOnFirstTenderShape", "statement": "A load is booked on its first tender: the row that does not point to an earlier row. A re-tender is not a second load."}, {"rule": "tw:LoadCountedOnceShape", "statement": "A load is one shipment, counted once: it has exactly one first tender."}, {"rule": "tw:RetenderShape", "statement": "A re-tender points to exactly one earlier tender. That first row keeps status RTND and is never deleted."}, {"rule": "tw:SiteRollsUpToOneCustomerShape", "statement": "A shipping site rolls up to exactly one parent account, which is its customer."}, {"rule": "tw:TenderAccountsShape", "statement": "The account on a load is a shipping site, and the account that pays is a bill-to party. Neither is the customer."}, {"rule": "tw:TestLoadsAreNeverBilledShape", "statement": "Test loads are never billed."}, {"rule": "tw:TestOrVoidIsNotALoadShape", "statement": "A test load or a voided load is not a load."}]}}, {"seq": 9, "tool": "lookup_definition", "arguments": {"term": "operations on-time"}, "response_id": "14b6bfd5-e95f-4094-b1cb-b4b73ec4c2bd", "contract_version": "2.0.0", "definitions": [{"id": "local_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}, {"id": "on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}, {"id": "portal_on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "Director of Customer Experience"}], "result": {"term": "operations on-time", "matches": [{"term": "tw:OnTime", "kind": "business term", "label": "on-time", "also_called": ["late", "late delivery", "on time", "on-time delivery rate", "on-time rate"], "definition": {"id": "on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}, "rules": ["A load is on time when the truck arrives at the final delivery stop at or before the end of the appointment window. Arriving early is on time.", "A load that arrived late and has a delay the shipper caused (a DLAY status event with reason SHPR) is left out of the measure, top and bottom. It is neither on time nor late.", "A load the shipper delayed that still arrived inside its window counts as on time.", "Arrival and appointment are compared on the same clock: local time at the facility.", "The rate is on-time loads divided by measured loads, over delivered loads.", "Two other meanings are in use and are not the official rate: operations watches arrival inside the appointment window for every delivered load, shipper-caused or not; and the customer portal uses its own rule."], "not_the_same_as": ["tw:PortalOnTime"], "warehouse_source": ["tms_stop: arr_ts, appt_end_lcl, tz_nm at the final delivery stop; tms_stat_evt: evt_cd = 'DLAY' with rsn_cd = 'SHPR'"]}, {"term": "tw:PortalOnTime", "kind": "business term", "label": "portal on-time", "also_called": ["customer portal on-time", "portal"], "definition": {"id": "portal_on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "Director of Customer Experience"}, "rules": ["It is the right answer only when the question is about what customers see in the portal. It is not the official on-time rate.", "The portal compares dates, not appointment times, and knows nothing about who caused a delay."], "not_the_same_as": ["tw:OnTime"], "warehouse_source": ["ptl_shpmt.on_time_ind"]}, {"term": "tw:LocalTime", "kind": "business term", "label": "local time", "also_called": ["UTC", "calendar day", "delivery date", "time zone"], "definition": {"id": "local_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}, "rules": ["A truck that arrives in the evening at its destination arrived on that local calendar day, although the stored UTC instant may fall on the next day.", "Appointment times are compared with arrival times only after putting both on the same clock.", "Booking dates use the UTC date of crt_ts. Financial dates (inv_dt, cr_dt, fee_dt) are plain dates and need no conversion.", "Every *_lcl column is a wall-clock time at the facility, with no zone attached. The zone is in tz_nm on the stop and on the facility.", "Every *_ts column is an instant stored in UTC."], "warehouse_source": ["*_ts columns (UTC); *_lcl columns with tz_nm"]}]}}, {"seq": 10, "tool": "compute_metric", "arguments": {"metrics": ["operations_on_time_rate", "on_time_rate"], "start_date": "2026-07-01", "end_date": "2026-09-30"}, "response_id": "8eca62ad-c7ad-4ed6-9535-061d917af660", "contract_version": "2.0.0", "definitions": [{"id": "on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}], "result": {"columns": ["operations_on_time_rate", "on_time_rate"], "rows": [[84.04193360512522, 87.58725341426404]], "row_count": 1, "truncated": false}}, {"seq": 11, "tool": "compute_metric", "arguments": {"where": ["delivery__arrived_on_time = false", "delivery__shipper_delayed = true"], "start_date": "2026-07-01", "metrics": ["delivered_loads"], "end_date": "2026-09-30"}, "response_id": "4228caa2-f0bf-4de4-a316-027e36adb401", "contract_version": "2.0.0", "definitions": [{"id": "delivered_load", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}], "result": {"columns": ["delivered_loads"], "rows": [[139]], "row_count": 1, "truncated": false}}, {"seq": 12, "tool": "compute_metric", "arguments": {"where": ["delivery__shipper_delayed = true"], "end_date": "2026-09-30", "metrics": ["late_deliveries"], "start_date": "2026-07-01"}, "response_id": "0c1053ac-5d86-42e3-bf21-fe85718ef23b", "contract_version": "2.0.0", "definitions": [{"id": "on_time", "version": 1, "owner": "VP Operations"}], "result": {"columns": ["late_deliveries"], "rows": [[0]], "row_count": 1, "truncated": 